-- ============================================================
-- ROLLBACK for 20260710190000_v5_claim_guest_scenario.sql
-- DO NOT APPLY except as a deliberate, Paul-approved rollback.
--
-- Scope: removes the RPC only. It does NOT (and cannot safely)
-- un-claim scenarios already stamped by executed claims:
-- reverting user_id to NULL would strip rows a real signed-in
-- user now legitimately owns (and whose turn/fact copies were
-- stamped in the same transaction). Executed claims are data,
-- not schema — reverting them is a separate, per-row decision
-- that must never ride a schema rollback.
--
-- If a per-row manual un-claim IS ever performed (user_id back to
-- NULL), it MUST also remove that scenario's `guest_claimed_<id>`
-- journey event from scenarios.events — otherwise a later honest
-- claim by a DIFFERENT user collides with the stale event's
-- claimed_user_id and fails 22023 via the default deterministic
-- event id (the re-claimer would have to pass a fresh p_event_id).
-- (Review fixup 2, 2026-07-10.)
-- ============================================================

DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS public.claim_guest_scenario(UUID, UUID, TEXT);
